  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  name: leocad\n  version: \"26.09\"\n\npackage:\n  name: ${{ name }}\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/leozide/leocad/archive/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 01c78e274cb2e3d496d6e904333f1cff88afb94929b5c9c7eb42bc018f3a530b\n  patches:\n    - ldraw-library-path.patch\n    - disable-macos-bundle.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 1\n  script: build.sh\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler(\"cxx\") }}\n    - ${{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n    - make\n    - if: linux\n      then:\n        # Required to link with libGL\n        - libglu\n        - ${{ cdt(\"mesa-libgl-devel\") }}\n        - ${{ cdt(\"mesa-dri-drivers\") }}\n        - ${{ cdt(\"libselinux\") }}\n        - ${{ cdt(\"libxdamage\") }}\n        - ${{ cdt(\"libxxf86vm\") }}\n        - ${{ cdt(\"libxext\") }}\n  host:\n    - qt-main\n    - ldraw-parts\n    - zlib\n    - if: linux\n      then:\n        - xorg-libxfixes\n  run:\n    - ldraw-parts\n\ntests:\n  - script:\n      - test -f $PREFIX/bin/leocad\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/leozide/leocad\n  repository: https://github.com/leozide/leocad\n  documentation: https://www.leocad.org/\n  license: GPL-2.0-only\n  license_file:\n    - docs/COPYING.txt\n  summary: A CAD program for creating virtual LEGO models\n  description: |\n    LeoCAD has an intuitive interface that is designed to allow\n    new users to start creating new models without having to spend\n    too much time learning the application.\n    At the same time, it has a rich feature set that\n    enables experienced users to build models by using\n    techniques that are more advanced.\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - SylvainCorlay\n    - derthorsten\n",
